name issue_368_tracker_outage_render
describe issue_268_freeze_rule_outage with rate_utilization_tracker on: after the 3 s outage the video recovers with one freeze, as libwebrtc (issue #368)
# With the tracker on, our receiver used to render the post-outage keyframe alone at ~14.7 s and then
# wait ~1.1 s for a retransmission of the next delta frame: seed 1 had 3 freezes, 6251 ms (main @ 55bf3d9).
# The retry interval of that NACK follows the receiver's RTT. libwebrtc's receiver measures it over
# XR RRTR/DLRR (modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_receiver.cc, video/video_receive_stream2.cc), and
# so does ours since #361; with it the stall after the keyframe is ~0.39 s and seed 1 has 1 freeze, 4641 ms.
# libwebrtc (parity-data traces, issue_268_freeze_rule_outage, tracker on as its default): 1 freeze on
# seeds 1-10, total 714-4969 ms. Ours seeds 1-10: 1 freeze on every seed, total 233-4641 ms.
seed 1
duration 40s
audio off
rate_utilization_tracker on
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s down
at 13s up
expect video.frames_rendered > 1000
expect video.freeze_count <= 1
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 5200
